Z||000000||Mach10||07-11-2001||01:59 PM||||I have the original unit off. The thing barely turns on it's own, and it leaks like a sieve. That was NOWHERE near as hard as I was afraid of  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Now, let's just wait until I snap a bolt putting the new one in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||07-11-2001||02:17 PM||||Just watch out for the small ones.  They don't need a lot of torque.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||07-12-2001||02:31 AM||||Woo-hoo! No broken bolts or ANYTHING  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000003||StuGood||07-12-2001||01:12 PM||||Going well?!  Wha - ??  You <B>must</B> be doing something wrong, Mach10!  You sure that's a <B>Fiero</B> you're working on?  You know those things require engine removal, and cutting and welding to replace the headlights, much less the water pump.  Lousy disposable cars!<P>Wait a minute... water pump?  Aren't those Fiarrroze air cooled?  I mean, they're just little plastic Corvairs, you know.  I know all about them pretty much firsthand, because my ex-girlfriend's hair stylist's 2nd husband had an casual aquaintance of his give their next-door-neighbor's (from where he used to live ten years ago) dog a ride to the vet in one, one time.  And the dog still sheds an awful lot (or so I heard), so obviously them Ferarro's is just plain no good.  <P>And here, you're <B>already</B> having to put a water pump in?  Man!<P>Enough already  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  Glad it's going well, and hope it stays that way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">             <P>       ||||reg||12
Z||000004||Mach10||07-12-2001||01:50 PM||||It's done, doesn't *SEEM* to leak (after small problem with thermostat and filler cap  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> ) and now that the belt's tight, runs nice.<P>Actually, besides being long, it wasn't too hard. The wheel bearings where the PITA. Try seating new races with nothing to press them in, nor a piece of pipe the right diameter to drift them in    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P><BR>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-12-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000005||Jason Kamrud||07-12-2001||10:01 PM||||Hey sounds like you're doing pretty well. I thought I was pretty lucky when I replaced my last water pump...I only broke off 3 bolts that time! But a little tin foil and ALOT of rtv silicone fixed that.  I wish GM would've put a little more effort into making the car a little easier to work on...that's a pain to have to take the wheel off & all that plastic wheel housing apart just for a water pump. But oh well, it's all in good fun anyways.  It's a small price to pay to drive one of Detroit's most exotic cars of all time.<P>------------------<BR>Jason Kamrud||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||07-13-2001||01:52 AM||||You know? I never did that! Just disassembled the battery tray, removed the battery, jacked the car up on stands, moved the sensors and vacuum lines, and went at it. The last 3 bolts were done while under the car. I was surprised how easy (but time-consuming) it was!||||reg||6
